### Where AI is Used (Architectural Specification)

| Aspect | Implementation Details |
| :--- | :--- |
| **Component Location** | `app/services/vision_parser_v2.py` (`VisionLayoutParserV2`) |
| **AI Model Used** | **OpenAI GPT-4o Multimodal Vision** |
| **Input to AI** | High-resolution rasterized rendering (150 DPI PNG) of the uploaded PDF's first page or uploaded template image + `MASTER_VISION_PROMPT`. |
| **Output from AI** | Machine-readable **Normalized YAML Layout Blueprint (`v2.0`)** containing geometric bounding boxes (`bbox` in a 0–1000 coordinate grid), page dimensions, typography metadata, color palettes, key-value field bindings, and tabular data column rules. |
| **Core Problem Solved by AI** | **Zero-Shot Document Ingestion**: Eliminates the need for manual, tedious coordinate measuring or hardcoded template mapping for each dealership. When a new dealer uploads a custom-designed quote template, the Vision LLM dynamically infers the visual layout, labels, and table structure on the fly. |
| **Resilience & Fallback Strategy** | If the OpenAI API key is missing or the external API call fails, the system automatically falls back to `_parse_pdf_structurally()` — a deterministic, rule-based layout analyzer using PyMuPDF span positions and coordinate heuristics. |

